<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamaguchi Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamaguchi Prefecture is the westernmost prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with its capital at Yamaguchi city and its largest city at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimonoseki">Shimonoseki</a>. It was formed in 1871 from the Chōshū domain of the Mōri clan, covering the old provinces of Suō and Nagato. Its men led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>, and it has produced more prime ministers of Japan than any other prefecture, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi">Itō Hirobumi</a>, Satō Eisaku and Abe Shinzō.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yamaguchi-prefecture.jpg" alt="Yamaguchi Prefecture" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: កៀនស្វាយ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B2%A9%E5%9B%BD%E5%9F%8E%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E8%A6%8B%E3%81%9F%E9%8C%A6%E5%B8%AF%E6%A9%8B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
